    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "At the center of the runway stood a vast, semi-transparent mirrored cube, inspired by Italian artist Luciano Fabro's installation *Cubo di specchi* (Mirror Cube). As models moved through the mirrored box, its diffused surfaces not only refracted layer upon layer of the garments' multiple silhouettes, but also forced the audience into an unavoidable exchange of glances with one another — transforming the act of watching a show into a social ritual of gazing at oneself and encountering others, all beneath a hypnotic visual spell.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
